# Rust
/target/
# Nested cargo build dirs (verification reproducers, sdk crates). The anchored
# rule above only covers the workspace root, so a reproducer's target/ was
# stageable — 173 build artefacts nearly went into a commit.
#
# The cost of the unanchored form, stated because it has been paid: it matches ANY
# directory named `target`, a Rust MODULE directory included. One was created under
# `mcp-re-proxy/src/.../registration/` and its new file was silently unstageable — the
# commit went out with a `mod flags;` resolving to nothing, and
# `scripts/bazel_srcs_gate.py` is what caught it rather than a person. Name a source
# module something else; the ignore stays unanchored because build artefacts are the
# larger hazard.
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Lean build output. `tools/verification/verify-lean` runs `lake build` in
# `verification/lean/`, which creates `.lake/` there — oleans and a resolved
# `lake-manifest.json`, hundreds of megabytes.
#
# The manifest is a BUILD ARTIFACT here, not a pin. Dependencies resolve out of the pinned
# extraction image's own package directory (`lakefile.toml`'s `packagesDir`), so what gets
# resolved is decided by the image digest in `verification/policy/toolchains.lock.toml`,
# and the publish workflow checks the image's mathlib against
# `[aeneas_lean_backend].mathlib_revision` before that digest is ever recorded. A second
# copy committed here would be a second answer to which mathlib a theorem was proved with.
/verification/lean/.lake/
/verification/lean/lake-manifest.json

# Bazel convenience symlinks (they point into ~/Library/Caches/bazel/).
#
# A GLOB, not four names. Bazel names one of them after the workspace DIRECTORY, so a build
# run from a worktree or a temporary checkout creates a symlink this list did not predict:
# `bazel-wt-capsule` was created in a scratch worktree, was matched by nothing here, and was
# committed — a tracked symlink (mode 120000) pointing at /private/tmp. It dangled on every
# other machine, and crashed `scripts/conformance_claims_gate.py` on any machine where
# something happened to exist at the path it named.
/bazel-*

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# work directory not to be tracked
/work/

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Coverage artifact from running the SDK suite at the repo root.
.coverage

# Claude Code
/.claude

# ADR-MCPRE-059 attestation store — derived evidence, never source (§"Evidence attestation").
/.verification/
